config MODU_OS_MODE_PERSIST
    bool "Remember the OS mode layer across reboots"
    default n
    depends on SETTINGS
    help
      Save the toggle state of the OS mode layer (macOS overlay) to settings
      and restore it on the next boot, so the keyboard comes back up in the
      mode it was left in.

      Only meaningful on the split central, which is the half that resolves
      the keymap.

config MODU_OS_MODE_LAYER
    int "Layer id of the OS mode overlay"
    default 1
    depends on MODU_OS_MODE_PERSIST
    help
      Must match the position of mac_layer in the keymap.

config MODU_OS_MODE_SAVE_DEBOUNCE_MS
    int "Milliseconds to debounce OS mode saves"
    default 500
    depends on MODU_OS_MODE_PERSIST
    help
      ZMK_SETTINGS_SAVE_DEBOUNCE defaults to 60s, which is tuned for settings
      that change often. Toggling the OS mode is a rare, deliberate action and
      the user may well power cycle right after it, so this is kept short
      enough that the change survives an immediate reboot.
